 9. **Uploaded content is inert.** Every R2 object response carries `nosniff` and a sandbox CSP; SVG is served as an attachment. Stored metadata cannot turn these off.
 10. **Billing is authenticated.** SetupIntents bind to the session's Stripe customer, browser writes reject foreign origins, and webhooks verify the raw body with a bounded timestamp. Request-time code links a Stripe customer to an account only by an id the account produced (Checkout owner metadata, a stored subscription or customer id), never by email.
 11. **Webhooks verify before they act.** Stripe, Mux and Resend signatures are checked over the raw body with a constant-time compare before any write. All three are router routes; Resend's is `POST /api/resend/webhook` (`workers/frontend-router/src/auth-email/webhook.ts`).
-12. **Agent calls carry an AuthKit bearer and never a cookie.** `POST /mcp` refuses a request that carries `clarity_session` at all, verifies RS256 against one issuer's JWKS with the audience pinned to `<origin>/mcp`, refuses impersonation (`act`) tokens, maps `sub` to an account through the same identity read the cookie path uses, and never exchanges the token for a session (`workers/frontend-router/src/agent/caller.ts`). The issuer is `AGENT_AUTH_ISSUER` per environment; a `pr-<n>` preview trusts its own origin as issuer only while `AGENT_PREVIEW_JWKS` names the preview signer's public key, and `scripts/deploy-config.test.sh` keeps that var off staging and production. The route table marks the path `bearer-only`, which is the one reason it skips the cross-origin mutation guard.
+12. **Agent calls carry an AuthKit bearer and never a cookie.** `POST /mcp` refuses a request that carries `clarity_session` at all, verifies RS256 against one issuer's JWKS with the audience pinned to `<origin>/mcp`, refuses impersonation (`act`) tokens, maps `sub` to an account through the same identity read the cookie path uses, and never exchanges the token for a session (`workers/frontend-router/src/agent/caller.ts`). The issuer is `AGENT_AUTH_ISSUER` per environment; a `pr-<n>` preview trusts its own origin as issuer only while `AGENT_PREVIEW_JWKS` names the preview signer's public key, and `scripts/deploy-config.test.sh` keeps that var off staging and production. The route table marks the path `bearer-only`, which is the one reason it skips the cross-origin mutation guard. Every `(sub, client_id)` pair is an Agent Connection row (`agent/connections.ts`): a revoked row refuses every token the pair presents, refreshed or not; once an owner has revoked anything, an unseen client waits `pending` for their approval; an account holds at most ten. Every non-read an agent makes passes one policy dispatcher (`agent/dispatch.ts`) that checks the permission, the per-connection limiter, entitlement (a read the router cannot complete answers 503, never open) and the replay store, then lands an `agent_actions` row. `/api/agent/*` is the owner's cookie-session side and refuses an impersonated session on every non-GET.
 
